{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OUTSTANDING-AC WORK STARTED. Pushed change 1053 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1053).\n\nDEFECT FOUND while setting up the live run — the reason AC(a) could not simply be \"dispatch and read the\noutput\". The `jira-dc-harness` job in .github/workflows/external-integration.yml installs `.[dev]`, and `dev`\nself-references only `[agents,metrics]` — NOT `[jira-datacenter]`. So `pycontribs/jira` was absent on that\nrunner and ALL FIVE tests in tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_transport.py skipped on their `_skip_no_extra`\nguard, while test_harness_smoke.py's 4 tests kept executing. Because the all-skip canary counts\ncollected-vs-executed GLOBALLY per session, the smoke tests executing MASKED the transport module's all-skip:\nthe job reported green having exercised no transport code whatsoever. Verified locally — `import jira` fails\nin a `.[dev]` venv.\n\nThat means the job's previous green runs are NOT evidence for this AC, and reporting them as such would have\ncertified untested code. Two fixes in 1053:\n 1. the DC job installs `.[dev,jira-datacenter]`;\n 2. \"harness reachable but extra absent\" is now a LOUD FAILURE rather than a skip (autouse fixture), so this\n    class of false green cannot recur. Truth table verified by direct evaluation:\n      extra=yes/harness=up   -> RUN        extra=yes/harness=down -> SKIP (via _skip)\n      extra=no /harness=up   -> FAIL-LOUD  extra=no /harness=down -> SKIP  (legitimate: plain dev checkout)\n\nAC(b) is also in 1053: live NameIdentity user-search coverage. Note what the code actually does, asserted\nrather than assumed — the two halves of that AC live in different places by design:\n * `_search_users_by_username` (backend.py) returns `(name, True, False)` for a real user — authoritative, the\n   live wire J4 left dangling. It had ZERO test coverage of any kind before this change.\n * for an UNKNOWN user it returns `(None, True, False)` — \"authoritative but unmappable\", which\n   `NameIdentity`/`_resolve` maps to `(\"\", True, False)` (desired-unassigned). It deliberately does NOT raise:\n   raising inside the resolver would break that state machine.\n * `BackendAssigneeNotFoundError` is raised on the APPLY path (`transport._assign`), which is where an unknown\n   assignee actually becomes an error. The new test asserts both halves live.\n\nAlso confirmed against the installed library (jira 3.10.5) that `search_users(user=...)` sends the `username`\nquery param — the Server/DC form — not Cloud's `query`, so the lookup is DC-correct.\n\nThis change must LAND before the AC evidence can be produced: workflow_dispatch runs from a GitHub ref, GitHub\nis a read-only mirror, and the Gerrit review ref creates no GitHub branch. So the sequence is submit 1053 ->\ndispatch external-integration.yml on main -> summarise the run here. Ticket stays in_progress until that\noutput exists."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785436566377569001,"uuid":"1d4fd337-258e-4aee-9361-865b79dc7a15"}